# Export-ignoring /.github blinds OSSF Scorecard's file-based checks
# (Dangerous-Workflow, Token-Permissions, Pinned-Dependencies report `-1` = "not
# applicable", not a penalty) — Scorecard analyses the export-ignored tarball.
# Accepted: those are covered on the real checkout by zizmor + CodeQL `actions`.
/.github            export-ignore
/.phplint.yml       export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/tests              export-ignore
/AGENTS.md          export-ignore
# The npm manifest carries devEngines, scripts and devDependencies that mean
# nothing to a Composer consumer, and `git archive` — which is what Packagist
# serves — shipped all of it. npm is unaffected: a `github:` dependency is packed
# by the `files` allow-list, which does not read .gitattributes. The template
# this package publishes already carries the line; the package lints itself with
# its own template, so it has to carry it too.
/package.json       export-ignore
